<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andriantsoly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1847">1847</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andriantsoly was the last independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakalava">Sakalava</a> king of Boina in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, a convert to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. When the Merina under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radama-i">Radama I</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahajanga">Mahajanga</a> in 1824 he fled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a> and later made himself ruler of Mayotte. Threatened by rivals, he sold the island to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1841 in return for a pension, giving France its first foothold in the archipelago.</p></div>
